<title>GERMANY: VW offers preferred shares to workforce.</title>
<headline>VW offers preferred shares to workforce.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen AG is to issue preferred shares worth a nominal 2.7 million marks ($1.7 million) to its workforce, the carmaker said in an announcement in Germany's Boersen-Zeitung newspaper on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 54,260 shares, which do not bear voting rights, each have a nominal value of 50 marks and carry an issue price of 436 marks per share, although VW employees can buy the shares at a discounted price of 286 marks.</p>
<p>Under terms of the issue, VW stands ready to buy the shares back at the issue price.</p>
<p>VW said the shares would probably be listed from January 31. ($ = 1.596 German Marks)</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
